title: TreeStart
---
//This dialogue will run using a random, making things more organized and clean
<<set $tree = random_range(1,11)>>

<<if $tree == 1>>
    {$charName}: This tree really brings the whole room together.
<<elseif $tree == 2>>
    {$charName}: I believe this tree will really have an impact on others and the future itself.
<<elseif $tree == 3>>
    {$charName}: Another memory to add onto this tree.
<<elseif $tree == 4>>
    {$charName}: I wonder how others will view these memories.
<<elseif $tree == 5>>
    {$charName}: This tree must be countless years old.
<<elseif $tree == 6>>
    {$charName}: Was this tree always here? Or was it just added along with everything else in the exhibit.
<<elseif $tree == 7>>
    {$charName}: If I look at these memories for too long, I may just burst into tears.
<<elseif $tree == 8>>
    {$charName}: Memories on a tree is definitely a way to do things.
<<elseif $tree == 9>>
    {$charName}: I wonder what kind of tree this is.
<<elseif $tree == 10>>
    {$charName}: The tree looks completely healthy. I guess the staff do a great job taking care of it.
<<else>>
    {$charName}: Another day of putting another memory on the tree.
<<endif>>
===